AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.
EOT
cat > "$dst/README.txt" <<EOT
xash3d-anniversary $version: Half-Life for Linux and the Steam Deck, with a menu made for a pad, speech subtitles
and three render styles (Original, Software, Enhanced) that switch on the fly.

You need Half-Life in Steam: nothing of the game is in this archive.
Unpack it anywhere you can write to and run ./xash3d-anniversary. On the Deck, add that file to Steam as a
non-Steam game. Add -gamepadui on a desktop for the pad menu; on the Deck it is the default. SDL2 comes from the system.

Source: https://github.com/18woldemar/xash3d-anniversary
Licences and where the art comes from are in licenses/. The speech captions are Fograin's Half-Life Subtitles MOD.
EOT

tar -C "$work" -czf "$out/$name-linux-amd64.tar.gz" "$name"
du -h "$out/$name-linux-amd64.tar.gz"
